WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.195 --> 00:00:02.212
You can clone, sync and run the whole

2
00:00:02.212 --> 00:00:04.695
fast test suite in a few commands.

3
00:00:04.695 --> 00:00:05.782
We'll go through them,

4
00:00:05.782 --> 00:00:07.120
look at real output,

5
00:00:07.120 --> 00:00:09.375
and find where the tests live.

6
00:00:09.820 --> 00:00:11.995
You need uv and nothing else.

7
00:00:11.995 --> 00:00:15.013
The sync command creates the environment and installs

8
00:00:15.013 --> 00:00:16.450
everything.

9
00:00:16.570 --> 00:00:18.795
The test run is the fast suite,

10
00:00:18.795 --> 00:00:21.708
and it needs no voice model or GPU.

11
00:00:21.708 --> 00:00:24.075
The third command starts the daemon with fake

12
00:00:24.075 --> 00:00:26.275
speech, so you can try the player without

13
00:00:26.275 --> 00:00:28.125
downloading a model.

14
00:00:28.570 --> 00:00:30.825
Collecting without running is a cheap way to

15
00:00:30.825 --> 00:00:32.445
see the shape of the suite.

16
00:00:32.445 --> 00:00:34.420
I trimmed the list to a few lines;

17
00:00:34.420 --> 00:00:36.650
the last line is real.

18
00:00:36.820 --> 00:00:39.525
Seven hundred eighty-two tests were collected in under

19
00:00:39.525 --> 00:00:40.745
half a second.

20
00:00:40.745 --> 00:00:43.375
Nothing ran, so this only proves the suite

21
00:00:43.375 --> 00:00:45.225
imports cleanly.

22
00:00:45.370 --> 00:00:47.182
The names say what is covered:

23
00:00:47.182 --> 00:00:49.900
themes, version agreement across manifests,

24
00:00:49.900 --> 00:00:51.850
and video export.

25
00:00:52.270 --> 00:00:54.620
CONTRIBUTING lists three more checks.

26
00:00:54.620 --> 00:00:56.975
The marked tests need real models or start

27
00:00:56.975 --> 00:00:59.725
processes, so run them when you touch speech

28
00:00:59.725 --> 00:01:01.250
or the daemon.

29
00:01:01.445 --> 00:01:03.707
Ruff checks lint and formatting.

30
00:01:03.707 --> 00:01:06.300
The Node command tests the player's pure timing

31
00:01:06.300 --> 00:01:09.200
logic, which lives in JavaScript.

32
00:01:09.670 --> 00:01:12.670
Real help output, with the descriptions shortened.

33
00:01:12.670 --> 00:01:14.883
Three commands matter most to you.

34
00:01:14.883 --> 00:01:17.720
Serve runs the daemon you will test against.

35
00:01:17.720 --> 00:01:20.570
Play voices a Markdown file by hand.

36
00:01:20.570 --> 00:01:22.000
Doctor is what to run,

37
00:01:22.000 --> 00:01:23.725
and paste into a bug report,

38
00:01:23.725 --> 00:01:25.950
when something misbehaves.

39
00:01:26.395 --> 00:01:28.508
Everything is under the tests folder,

40
00:01:28.508 --> 00:01:31.225
one file per area of the source.

41
00:01:31.345 --> 00:01:35.207
Parser tests such as format blocks cover format.py.

42
00:01:35.207 --> 00:01:37.570
Build slides covers build.py,

43
00:01:37.570 --> 00:01:39.420
and store covers sessions.

44
00:01:39.420 --> 00:01:43.375
The MCP server file exercises the tools.

45
00:01:43.570 --> 00:01:46.620
Versions fails whenever the manifests disagree,

46
00:01:46.620 --> 00:01:48.763
which is why you run the sync script

47
00:01:48.763 --> 00:01:50.433
after bumping a version.

48
00:01:50.433 --> 00:01:52.920
The player's logic is tested separately,

49
00:01:52.920 --> 00:01:54.950
in the js folder.
